/* *   EventHandlers.incl - what happens when the user does something * *   Starting template from App Builder for FutureBasic: created once, then *   yours.  Regeneration never overwrites it (delete it to get a fresh copy). *   <project>.main registers these three functions with FutureBasic's event loop: *       on appevent fn DoAppEvent      the application (launch, quit, ...) *       on menu     fn DoMenu          a menu choice *       on dialog   fn DoDialog        anything in a window: clicks, table selections, ... * *   Developer notes *   - The generated behaviour lives in other files; each handler below passes the event *     on, in order, until one says "mine" (returns YES).  Put your own handling before a *     call (to change what happens) or after it (to add to it). *   - DoDialog's order:  the window frame (App Shell.incl: navigation, theme menu)  -> *     the pages (App Pages.incl: lists, forms, New / Save / Delete / Refresh)  ->  Log In. *   - ev, tag and wnd: the event (_btnClick, _tableViewSelectionDidChange, ...), the tag of *     the control it came from (Model Tags.incl names every generated one), the window. *   - The same file works in both editions: Lite (SQLite in the app) and Enterprise (an *     API Logic Server).  The pages reach the data through App Data, never directly. */// fblint: these are in App Pages.incl, which the generator writes beside this file// generated: AppPagesDoDialog, AppPagesDoMenu, AppPagesLoginvoid local fn DoAppEvent( ev as long )fn ShellDoAppEvent( ev )                   // quit when the window closesend fnvoid local fn DoMenu( menuID as long, itemID as long )if ( fn AppPagesDoMenu( menuID, itemID ) ) then exit fn   // Records: New, Save, Delete, Refresh// your own menus hereend fn// the header's Log In button (shown only when the app signs in to a server: Enterprise)void local fn DoLoginfn AppPagesLoginend fnvoid local fn DoDialog( ev as long, tag as long, wnd as long )if ( fn ShellDoDialog( ev, tag, wnd ) ) then exit fn          // navigation and the theme menuif ( fn AppPagesDoDialog( ev, tag, wnd ) ) then exit fn       // lists, forms and the page actionsif ( ev == _btnClick && tag == _shellLoginButton )fn DoLoginexit fnend if// your own controls hereend fn